{
  "evidence_boundary": "Post-capture ship-pair recomposition diagnostic. Active membership and factual opponent rank are inherited from the separately validated mutable-history gate. Captured T-1 mission/Primary Enemy are never allowed to initiate the new-owner engagement. The factual opponent uses its independently reconstructed T-1 orders and strict diplomacy permission. Pair eligibility/phase is recomputed through production decide_ship_combat_pair under two captured-Friendly-Code bounds: the T-1 FC and a guaranteed nonmatching symbolic FC; phase is accepted only if invariant. LEFT/RIGHT is not promoted here. Instead, four competing side controls are compared independently: capture-side carry, generic opponent-initiator-right, frozen T-1 combat priority, and neutral captured orders with preserved/fresh FC. Elapsed factual VCRs before N+1 may supply pair occurrence history; N+1 supplies only the held-out side comparator.",
